/-!
# Finite completed differentials and the completed conormal sequence

Source: EGA IV-1, 0_IV 20.7.14--20.7.15, 20.7.20 and 21.9.1
(blueprint: lem-per-completed-differential-finite-conormal).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v w

open scoped TensorProduct

namespace KaehlerDifferential

/-- Completed differentials are finite, generated by exact differentials, and represent
all derivations to finite complete modules. Quotients have the completed conormal sequence;
localizing that sequence at a reduced minimal prime gives the canonical isomorphism.
Tensor factors are written with the scalar algebra first, using the canonical symmetry
from the order in the source. The two conormal arrows and the final equivalence are
specified on differential generators, so they are the canonical maps, not arbitrary maps.
The scalar structure on each target of a derivation is the one induced from its A-module
structure, expressed by `IsScalarTower`.

Source: EGA IV-1, 0_IV 20.7.14--20.7.15, 20.7.20 and 21.9.1
(blueprint: lem-per-completed-differential-finite-conormal).

Proof:
1. Choose generators t_i of the maximal ideal and lifts a_j of an F-basis of the finite
   residue extension. The ordinary conormal sequence
   (lem-weil-pbc-jacobi-zariski-differential-maps) shows that dt_i and da_j generate
   Omega modulo the maximal ideal; use d(sum u_i t_i) = sum u_i dt_i modulo m Omega.
2. Completion preserves these residue quotients and is complete and separated by
   lem-weil-pbc-module-completion-complete. The strengthened complete Nakayama lemma
   lem-weil-pbc-finite-over-complete-ring says the particular lifted differentials generate
   the completion. Thus it is finite without assuming ordinary Omega is finite.
3. A derivation corresponds to a linear map Omega to N. This preserves m^n multiples,
   so maps compatible sequences to compatible sequences. Completeness of N gives a
   linear map from the completion. It extends the derivation, and uniqueness follows
   from the differential generators of step 2. This proves the asserted bijection.
4. For proper I, the quotient C is finite over A, hence complete by
   lem-weil-pbc-finite-module-complete-over-complete-noetherian. It is Noetherian local,
   F embeds in C, and its residue extension is unchanged, so steps 1--3 apply to C.
5. Identify P = C tensor M with M/IM by the tensor universal property. Leibniz shows
   a mod I^2 maps well-definedly to 1 tensor da. Quotient P by this image to obtain Q.
   It is finite and complete by the same finite-module completeness theorem. The map
   a maps to [1 tensor da] descends to an F-derivation C to Q.
6. Universality from step 3 gives M_F(C) to Q. Conversely d_C composed with A to C
   gives M to M_F(C), factoring through P and Q. These maps fix differential generators
   in both directions, hence are inverse. This proves exactness and surjectivity.
7. At a reduced minimal prime q, lem-weil-pbc-minimal-prime-reduced-localization-field
   gives q A_q = 0 and A_q = Frac(A/q). Thus (q/q^2) tensor Frac(A/q) vanishes:
   each a in q is killed by a denominator outside q. Apply
   lem-weil-pbc-tensor-right-exact to step 6 and reassociate tensor products. The resulting
   isomorphism sends l tensor da to l tensor d(a mod q), as asserted. -/
theorem completed_differential_finite_conormal
    (F : Type u) [Field F] (A : Type v) [CommRing A] [Algebra F A]
    [IsLocalRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A]
    [Module.Finite F (IsLocalRing.ResidueField A)] :
    Module.Finite A
      (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) (KaehlerDifferential F A)) ∧
    Submodule.span A (Set.range (fun a : A =>
      AdicCompletion.of (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) (KaehlerDifferential F A)
        (KaehlerDifferential.D F A a))) = ⊤ ∧
    (∀ (N : Type w) [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N] [Module F N]
      [IsScalarTower F A N] [Module.Finite A N]
      [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) N],
      Function.Bijective (fun f :
        AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) (KaehlerDifferential F A) →ₗ[A] N =>
        (f.comp (AdicCompletion.of (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
          (KaehlerDifferential F A))).compDer (KaehlerDifferential.D F A))) ∧
    (∀ (I : Ideal A), I ≠ ⊤ →
      IsAdicComplete ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) (A ⧸ I) ∧
      ∃ (δ : I.Cotangent →ₗ[A ⧸ I]
          (A ⧸ I) ⊗[A]
            AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) (KaehlerDifferential F A))
        (q : (A ⧸ I) ⊗[A]
            AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) (KaehlerDifferential F A) →ₗ[A ⧸ I]
          AdicCompletion ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))
            (KaehlerDifferential F (A ⧸ I))),
        (∀ a : I, δ (I.toCotangent a) = (1 : A ⧸ I) ⊗ₜ[A]
          AdicCompletion.of (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) (KaehlerDifferential F A)
            (KaehlerDifferential.D F A a)) ∧
        (∀ (a : A) (c : A ⧸ I),
          q (c ⊗ₜ[A] AdicCompletion.of (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
            (KaehlerDifferential F A) (KaehlerDifferential.D F A a)) =
          c • AdicCompletion.of ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I))
            (KaehlerDifferential F (A ⧸ I))
            (KaehlerDifferential.D F (A ⧸ I) (Ideal.Quotient.mk I a))) ∧
        Function.Exact δ q ∧ Function.Surjective q) ∧
    (IsReduced A → ∀ (p : Ideal A) [p.IsPrime], p ∈ minimalPrimes A →
      ∃ e : FractionRing (A ⧸ p) ⊗[A]
          AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) (KaehlerDifferential F A) ≃ₗ[
            FractionRing (A ⧸ p)]
        FractionRing (A ⧸ p) ⊗[A ⧸ p]
          AdicCompletion ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk p))
            (KaehlerDifferential F (A ⧸ p)),
        ∀ (a : A) (l : FractionRing (A ⧸ p)),
          e (l ⊗ₜ[A] AdicCompletion.of (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
            (KaehlerDifferential F A) (KaehlerDifferential.D F A a)) =
          l ⊗ₜ[A ⧸ p]
            AdicCompletion.of ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk p))
              (KaehlerDifferential F (A ⧸ p))
              (KaehlerDifferential.D F (A ⧸ p) (Ideal.Quotient.mk p a))) := by
  sorry

end KaehlerDifferential
